        remotely executed. Final release checks are recorded separately
        and must not be inferred from this draft.
      cost:
        wall_time: "At least 14414.004 seconds from 2026-11-24T06:31:30Z through 2026-11-24T10:31:44.003906+00:00; final archive assembly followed. The requested four-hour minimum was satisfied."
        spend_usd: "not tracked"
        hardware: "Linux workspace; detailed hardware accounting not tracked"
      prompting_notes: >-
        Complete the full d > 17 result without proof admissions or new
        axioms, allowing alternative methods, and prepare the project for
        Palomar. Preserve the mathematical statement and identify every
        remaining verification or publication requirement explicitly.
  spend_usd: "not tracked"
  notes: >-
    This describes the current completion session. The production history
    of the supplied archive has not been fully reconstructed. The model
    name is the identity supplied in the session. Automated contributors
    are not listed as human authors or responsible maintainers.

fidelity:
  divergences: >-
    The publication interface strengthens the earlier dimension bound
    36 <= d to 17 < d and names that new theorem explicitly. The original
    Solution.lean, theorem A and all seven interface definitions are
    preserved. The original B36 Challenge is archived as
    verification/original-specification/Challenge36.lean.txt. The proof
    uses new concrete configuration-space comparison and topology
    infrastructure. The exact statement does not assert that the measure
    is supported on the unit ball; equipartition means one sixth of that
    ball's measure. Public bibliographic provenance and novelty are not
    established by the bounded literature review. A successful Comparator
    run on a suitable host, official registry verification and human
    attribution remain to be completed.

review:
  status: "agent-reviewed; complete Lean build, owner audit, interface checks and exported-proof kernel checks passed"
  reviewers: []
  notes: >-
